# What belongs in this repository: the code that runs an experiment, the tests
# that pin its behaviour, and the per-run write-ups under
# biophysical-fusion/results/ that record what each run found. Nothing else.
#
# Everything a run *produces* — result JSON, summary/fold CSVs, figures, .npz
# arrays, saved models, executed notebooks, raw job logs — stays on the
# filesystem. The output trees below each carry their own .gitignore, written as
# an ALLOWLIST (`*` then targeted `!` lines) so a new output format cannot leak
# in by default:
#
#   biophysical-fusion/results/     per-run README.md, submit.sh, run scripts
#   biophysical-fusion/slurm_logs/  nothing — raw job output only
#   mdcnn_eval/                     the MD-CNN reproduction's code and params
#   h1_repro/                       the leak-reproduction scripts
#   regulatory_msa/                 the promoter-MSA generators
#
# The one class of generated text that IS tracked: results/**/*.md. A run's
# write-up is what preserves it. results/experiments/alllocus_run/ — 221 jobs,
# ~350 GPU-hours — was deleted with no copy anywhere, and only its README
# survives it.

# --- editor / interpreter noise ---------------------------------------------
.claude*
*__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- another project's repository -------------------------------------------
# The upstream benchmark, cloned here and only ever read (single point of
# contact: biophysical-fusion/bigtb_ref.py). It has its own remote, and 129 MB
# of WHO catalogues and GenBank references do not belong on ours. It was
# committed as a gitlink with no .gitmodules, so a clone got an empty directory
# regardless.
Big-TB-benchmark/

# --- third-party reference material -----------------------------------------
# Published papers, advisor slides, meeting notes: 15 MB of other people's PDFs,
# not ours to redistribute.
reference_docs/

# --- prose ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One README describes the project. Run write-ups are re-included by
# biophysical-fusion/results/.gitignore; everything else — TODOs, cleanup
# reports, paper drafts — is working text that does not need a remote.
*.md
!/biophysical-fusion/README.md
*.tex

# --- machine-readable output -------------------------------------------------
# Result payloads, job manifests, metrics dumps. Every .json in this tree is
# written by a script, never by hand.
*.json

# --- arrays, caches, saved models -------------------------------------------
*.npz
*.npy
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.keras
*.ckpt
*.pb
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib

# --- executed notebooks ------------------------------------------------------
# Every notebook is rendered by its scripts/build_<name>.py and carries its
# outputs inline (results.ipynb alone is 2.1 MB). The builder is the source.
*.ipynb

# --- rasters of tracked vectors ---------------------------------------------
# biophysical-fusion/diagrams/ keeps the .svg; the .png beside it is a render.
*.png

# AlphaFold C-alpha coordinates for the `structure` modality (small, public
# CC-BY 4.0 data): tracked so a fresh clone runs. raw/ PDBs are a re-fetchable cache.
!/structures/alphafold/*.npz
!/structures/alphafold/manifest.json
# LocusFusion v4: its README, the binding-site definitions and the distance table
# built from them (small), and the augmentation exclusion list -- inputs, not output
!/biophysical-fusion/locusfusion_v4/README.md
!/biophysical-fusion/locusfusion_v4/augment_exclusions.json
!/biophysical-fusion/locusfusion_v4/binding_sites/sites.json
!/biophysical-fusion/locusfusion_v4/binding_sites/distances.npz
!/biophysical-fusion/locusfusion_v4/binding_sites/distances.json
/structures/alphafold/raw/
# gene_msa window definitions (config, not data); aligned/ and slurm_logs/ stay out
!/gene_msa/gene_windows.json
/gene_msa/aligned/
/gene_msa/slurm_logs/
/gene_msa/who_t12_genotypes/

# --- workspace data, weights and frozen code snapshots ----------------------
# Inputs and outputs that live on /scratch only: model weights, token caches,
# genotype snapshots, the repaired MSAs, and the frozen code copies that sweep
# jobs run from (each holds its own BASE_COMMIT + working_tree.patch).
/model_weights_*/
/token_cache_*/
/data_snapshot/
/v3_snapshot/
/v3md_snapshot/
/v4_snapshot/
/lineage_snapshot/
/curated_fix/
/gene_msa/aligned_fixed/
/structures/ribosome/
*.pdf
